1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,492
Two teenagers built a seven billion dollar company out of a grocery app that failed.

2
00:00:04,492 --> 00:00:06,844
Then the stock market looked at it and said:

3
00:00:06,844 --> 00:00:07,700
four and a half.

4
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,740
This is how Zepto got so big, so fast, and why it still isn't on the stock market.

5
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:14,256
It starts in 2020.

6
00:00:14,256 --> 00:00:18,755
Aadit Palicha and Kaivalya Vohra are childhood friends who grew up in Dubai.

7
00:00:18,755 --> 00:00:22,130
They've just got into Stanford to study computer science.

8
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:23,684
Then the pandemic hits.

9
00:00:23,684 --> 00:00:27,140
They're stuck at home in Mumbai, and they can't get groceries delivered.

10
00:00:27,590 --> 00:00:30,030
So, still teenagers, they build Kirana Kart.

11
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:31,084
The idea is simple.

12
00:00:31,084 --> 00:00:34,910
Partner with local kirana shops and deliver their stock to your door.

13
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,346
It doesn't take off.

14
00:00:36,346 --> 00:00:42,210
Local shops run out of stock, they don't track inventory, and every order depends on a shopkeeper picking up the phone.

15
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:44,985
But the two of them don't go back to Stanford.

16
00:00:44,985 --> 00:00:48,270
An investor called Contrary offers to back them if they drop out.

17
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:49,230
They take the deal.

18
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:53,176
In 2021 they shut Kirana Kart down and start again.

19
00:00:53,176 --> 00:00:53,793
New name:

20
00:00:53,793 --> 00:00:54,204
Zepto.

21
00:00:54,204 --> 00:00:55,026
New promise:

22
00:00:55,026 --> 00:00:56,740
groceries in ten minutes.

23
00:00:57,190 --> 00:00:58,095
Here's the trick.

24
00:00:58,095 --> 00:00:59,374
Zepto doesn't use shops.

25
00:00:59,374 --> 00:01:04,114
It builds its own small warehouses, called dark stores, packed into dense neighbourhoods.

26
00:01:04,114 --> 00:01:05,233
No customers walk in.

27
00:01:05,233 --> 00:01:07,150
They only exist to pack orders fast.

28
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:12,045
Each dark store covers a small radius, so the rider only has a short distance to go.

29
00:01:12,045 --> 00:01:18,448
Aadit Palicha once pointed out that covering 1.8 kilometres in ten minutes means riding under fifteen kilometres an hour.

30
00:01:18,448 --> 00:01:22,470
The speed comes from where the store sits, not from how fast the rider goes.

31
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:24,842
And the stock is narrow on purpose.

32
00:01:24,842 --> 00:01:28,577
Not everything, just the few thousand items people actually reorder.

33
00:01:28,577 --> 00:01:30,170
Milk, bread, chips, chargers.

34
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:31,862
Investors loved it.

35
00:01:31,862 --> 00:01:38,200
Zepto was backed by Y Combinator, and by August 2023 it became India's first unicorn of the year.

36
00:01:38,650 --> 00:01:40,297
Then the money came in waves.

37
00:01:40,297 --> 00:01:45,465
In 2024, six hundred and sixty-five million dollars at a three point six billion valuation.

38
00:01:45,465 --> 00:01:49,610
A few months later, three hundred and fifty million more at five billion.

39
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:56,525
In October 2025, a US pension fund called Calpers led a four hundred and fifty million dollar round.

40
00:01:56,525 --> 00:01:59,240
Zepto was now worth seven billion dollars.

41
00:01:59,690 --> 00:02:01,436
On paper, the growth was insane.

42
00:02:01,436 --> 00:02:06,782
In the year ending March 2026, Zepto made twenty-two thousand six hundred crore rupees in revenue.

43
00:02:06,782 --> 00:02:09,510
It ran eleven hundred and thirty-nine dark stores.

44
00:02:09,510 --> 00:02:13,110
Nearly forty-eight million people ordered at least once that year.

45
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:17,570
In the last quarter of that year, it was handling over twenty-three lakh orders a day.

46
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:19,720
So why isn't it public?

47
00:02:20,170 --> 00:02:21,713
Because revenue isn't profit.

48
00:02:21,713 --> 00:02:23,469
Ten minute delivery is expensive.

49
00:02:23,469 --> 00:02:30,600
You pay rent for stores in prime locations, you pay riders, and you pay discounts to win customers from Blinkit, Instamart and Amazon.

50
00:02:31,050 --> 00:02:36,051
In the year before, Zepto's losses widened to over three thousand three hundred crore rupees.

51
00:02:36,051 --> 00:02:37,880
It was burning cash every quarter.

52
00:02:38,330 --> 00:02:45,031
Zepto filed for its IPO in December 2025 and got approval from Sebi in May 2026.

53
00:02:45,031 --> 00:02:47,460
The plan was to list in July.

54
00:02:47,910 --> 00:02:49,949
But Indian fund managers pushed back.

55
00:02:49,949 --> 00:02:51,658
Zepto only does quick commerce.

56
00:02:51,658 --> 00:02:57,060
It doesn't have a food delivery business like Swiggy or Zomato's parent, Eternal, to fall back on.

57
00:02:57,510 --> 00:02:59,799
So in July 2026, Zepto pulled the brakes.

58
00:02:59,799 --> 00:03:07,057
Instead of listing, it raised around a thousand crore rupees privately, at a valuation of roughly four and a half billion dollars.

59
00:03:07,057 --> 00:03:09,290
That's about a third less than its peak.

60
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:12,620
The IPO was pushed back by two to three quarters.

61
00:03:13,070 --> 00:03:14,790
Here's the part most people miss.

62
00:03:14,790 --> 00:03:15,832
Zepto isn't failing.

63
00:03:15,832 --> 00:03:20,940
Its cash burn came down, it says it has no debt, and it still has thousands of crores in the bank.

64
00:03:21,390 --> 00:03:24,223
What happened is the gap between two kinds of money.

65
00:03:24,223 --> 00:03:27,164
Private investors pay for what a company could become.

66
00:03:27,164 --> 00:03:29,180
Public markets pay for what it earns.

67
00:03:29,630 --> 00:03:32,634
Zepto proved that Indians want groceries in ten minutes.

68
00:03:32,634 --> 00:03:35,960
What it still has to prove is that ten minutes can make money.

69
00:03:36,410 --> 00:03:39,850
And the two people who have to prove it are still in their mid-twenties.

70
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:44,219
If Zepto lists in 2027, this might be the cheapest it ever looks.

71
00:03:44,219 --> 00:03:45,546
Or the most expensive.

72
00:03:45,546 --> 00:03:48,380
Tell me in the comments which one you'd bet on.

73
00:03:48,830 --> 00:03:51,223
And if you want the next breakdown, subscribe.

74
00:03:51,223 --> 00:03:52,420
I'm doing Blinkit next.
